WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:04.460
Deadpool is one of superhero comics' most
unlikely success stories.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.320
The crass, violent mercenary has gone from
a cult favorite to the face of a smash hit

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.430
film franchise.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.900
But while Deadpool's antics on the big screen
have been hilarious, not everything in the

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.559
comics has been quite so funny.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:18.130
Here's a look at some things Marvel wants
you to forget about Deadpool.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.720
He's a murderous psychopath

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.980
In the movies, Deadpool is a killer with a
conscience.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.380
In Marvel's head-scratchingly popular Deadpool
Kills line of comics, though, he just ruthlessly

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.449
murders everyone he can get his hands on.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:32.059
Among the most gruesome distasteful moments
is when he straight up murdered his friend

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:35.670
Spider-Man - by shooting him in the face - and
then there was the time he slaughtered the

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.690
X-Men and then wore Beast's furry skin like
a coat.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.710
Once Marvel Comics finished having Deadpool
psychotically slaughter its own roster of

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:46.420
characters, they had him move on to other
characters, this time from the pages of famous

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:52.030
works of literature, wantonly butchering everyone
from Moby Dick to Ebenezer Scrooge to Bagheera

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.510
from the Jungle Book.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.519
"That's gross."

00:00:55.519 --> 00:00:57.079
He's in love with death

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:01.299
In the Marvel Universe, Death takes the form
of a woman, and is most often seen being courted

00:01:01.299 --> 00:01:03.199
by the big purple one himself, Thanos.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:07.740
But during Wade's time under experimentation
in the Weapon X program, he finds himself

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.829
frequently so close to dying that he can see
and communicate with her - and he falls in

00:01:11.829 --> 00:01:14.430
love, trying to die just to be with her.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:18.840
However, Death's jealous ex Thanos eventually
uses his powers to make Deadpool immortal,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.159
keeping him away from Death permanently.

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:25.109
Considering Deadpool's romance with Vanessa
is the soul of the first film, chances are

00:01:25.109 --> 00:01:29.320
good you won't see her and the living embodiment
of mortality squaring off in any upcoming

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.780
Deadpool flicks.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.219
He's served himself as a cannibalistic snack

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:37.609
For a time, Deadpool was a member of the Uncanny
X-Force, a team that took care of the tasks

00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:39.430
too dirty for the X-Men to face.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.290
"We will be known as…

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.290
X-Force!"

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.939
"Isn't that a little derivative?"

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:45.549
"You're absolutely right!"

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:50.259
At the end of a particularly brutal battle,
Deadpool's teammate Archangel finds himself

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:51.280
in rough shape.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.369
To help nurse him back to health, Deadpool
ends up feeding Archangel chunks of Deadpool's

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:59.609
own flesh - in order to lend Archangel some
of Deadpool's superhuman healing factor.

00:01:59.609 --> 00:02:03.159
It works, but it's also… incredibly disturbing.

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:04.619
He's basically a complete ripoff

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:09.009
While it's been an open secret among comic
book collectors for decades, it might surprise

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:13.319
fans of the Deadpool movies to learn that
the character is actually a complete and intentional

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:18.659
ripoff of the DC Comics character Deathstroke,
who predated Deadpool by several years.

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:22.720
Deadpool creator Rob Liefeld was such a huge
fan of Deathstroke that he copied not just

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.799
the costume an d weapon choice, but the character's
name as well.

00:02:25.799 --> 00:02:27.210
Deadpool, Deathstroke...

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.220
you get the idea.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.510
Writer Fabian Niceiza figured Liefeld's ripoff
was so obvious they might as well just acknowledge

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.510
it.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:38.980
So, he decided to give Deadpool's secret identity
the name Wade Wilson as an homage to Deathstroke,

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.599
whose real name is Slade Wilson.

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:44.650
Hey, subtlety has never exactly been a strong
suit for Mr. Pool.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.790
His mental health issues are played for laughs

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:50.330
Given that he's a murderous psychopath who
thinks killing is hilarious, is in love with

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:54.060
death, and promotes cannibalism, it's pretty
safe to say that Deadpool has some fairly

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.420
serious mental health issues.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.510
Unfortunately, in the comics, those issues
are played for laughs when he ends up choosing

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.250
reformed supervillain Doctor Bong for a therapist.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.879
And that's kinda not even the worst part.

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:07.900
Marvel has consistently portrayed mental health
professionals as literal supervillains who

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.099
manipulate people in need for their own ends.

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:13.760
So look, Deadpool is really funny...but his
mental health struggles kind of aren't.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.910
Especially when, as part of his "therapy,"
Deadpool sucker punched Kitty Pryde.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:22.650
It wasn't even as funny as Doctor Bong's classic
appearances as Howard the Duck's archenemy.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.689
Talk about things Marvel would really like
movie fans to forget!

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:29.250
"You think I might find happiness in the animal
kingdom, Ducky?"

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.439
"Like they say, doll: 'Love's strange.'

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:35.340
We could always give it a try!"

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.349
"That's gross."

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.910
Thanks for watching!

